      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **Another dose.** If so, tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose is intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
